Create the DARK THEME variant of this exact four-pane DEPTH AI desktop reference. Change theme colors only, preserving the geometry, relative sizes, content, control positions, module positions, search, console and chat input. This is not a new layout.

Four persistent quadrants MUST remain simultaneously visible:
top left = large project preview;
bottom left = Console & Meta CLI, both console output and conversation visible;
top right = spatial Module canvas;
bottom right = Hierarchy & quick switch with search and Recent list.

Use neutral dark slate for application toolbar and hierarchy, deep blue-gray for module drafting surface, near-black for console/chat, and a distinctly lighter slate viewport surface for the checkout preview. Give each pane its own easily perceptible material and boundary, without glow. Convert the example checkout into a readable dark theme too: warm white text on dark slate cart/summary, product photos remain photographs, selected Total96 framed in apricot, prices readable. Module bodies have muted blue/sage fills with enough lightness or darkness difference for high readability; all module labels warm white on dark plates. Selected CalculateTotal is warm burnt-orange with readable light text. Preserve chamfered method bodies, register-shaped state bodies, open class-corner brackets. No neon.

Keep source/selection structure and bottom hierarchy. Mark Dark selected and Light unselected. Keep only selected graph relations as currently shown. Retain "Example conversation" and "DESIGN REFERENCE". Change the module caption to "Selected links · context retained" to avoid an unsupported exact-completeness claim. Remove the tiny arrowhead at the source end of the ApplyCoupon connector, leaving an arrowhead only at the CalculateTotal destination. No invented successes, no added metrics, no modal overlays.
